  "blocker": "The meta label is the conjunction of three near-independent base-model correctness events (crop RF correct AND classical yield within +/-25% per hectare AND seed RF correct). Its rate is the product of the three leg accuracies, and the classical yield leg passes on only 50.68% of the frozen test rows, which caps the task's success rate at 45.00% before any learner is involved. The determiners of each leg (true crop label, true yield per hectare, true seed label) are absent from the feature vector, which holds only base-model outputs. Measured evidence: 1-NN grouped CV on TRAIN scores 50.34% against a 50.40% majority baseline, and a label-permutation control scores 54.32% against a 55.00% test majority, so the features carry almost no label information. Reaching 85% would require the yield leg alone to pass on 95.1% of rows (now 50.7%). This is a target-definition and base-leg problem, not a meta-learner problem.",
